**Content correctness reminders** (engine-side
``stage_tool_allowlist['kickoff:action']`` restricts you to
``workhub_add_meeting_decision`` + ``workhub_get_document`` +
``workhub_list_documents`` + ``workhub_comment`` + ``read`` + ``think``
+ ``finish`` — registryhub_register_*, write/edit/apply_patch, wait,
polling are NOT in the surface, so you can't accidentally register
endpoints or write code during this kickoff):

- Reference only `user_flow` ids in `screens[i].user_flow` that you ALSO declare in your own `user_flows` list. Both halves live in YOUR section — keep them in lockstep within a single decision.
- Frontend's role at kickoff is to DECLARE the screen's api needs by `endpoint_id`; the orchestrator synthesizes the merged draft and registers endpoints itself once cross-check + arbitration pass.

**Stop rule** — call `finish()` immediately after `workhub_add_meeting_decision` returns (file-first form included). Do NOT cancel or fail any workhub tasks during kickoff — impl.* tasks are the orchestrator's dispatch plan for the next phase. Without `finish()`, the runtime will keep stepping you and you may double-record. ONE decision per (section, agent) per meeting round; the synthesizer uses the LAST recorded decision per pair if arbitration causes a revision.

FINAL PROTOCOL (this overrides anything above if in doubt): declare your section ONE ITEM PER CALL with the typed declare tools — they merge automatically. 1) read the requirements; 2) `kickoff_declare_ui_page(meeting_id='{{ meeting_id }}', milestone_index={{ milestone_index }}, id='<page_id>', route='/<route>', purpose='...', components=['<ChildComponentId>', ...], must_have=['<key visible element>', ...])` — ONCE PER PAGE (placeholders shown — derive every value from THIS app's requirements, never copy a domain shape; include component='<RootComponent>' and apis_used=[...] — they drive the page lifecycle); 2b) `kickoff_declare_ui_component(meeting_id='{{ meeting_id }}', milestone_index={{ milestone_index }}, id='...', component='...', kind='...', apis_used=[...], children=[...])` — REQUIRED, ONCE PER REUSABLE COMPONENT (NOT optional): decompose every page into components. RULE: a page that renders a LIST / GRID / FEED of repeated items MUST declare the repeated item as a ui_component (the card / row / tile) and list its id in that page's `components=[...]`; shared chrome (nav rail / sidebar, top bar, search box) MUST also be declared as components. Do NOT build pages as monoliths — a kickoff that declares ui_pages but ZERO ui_components is wrong and under-builds the UI. Components own the API calls they make; 3) one small `workhub_add_meeting_decision(..., decision={'section':'frontend','content':{'done_def': [...], 'feature_inventory': [...]}})` for the scalar fields — `done_def` / `feature_inventory` ONLY. Do NOT include `auth` (authentication is FRAMEWORK-OWNED — the generated stack provides /auth/* + JWT — and a decision carrying an `auth` key is REJECTED as wrong-keys) and do NOT declare `user_flows` (RETIRED: critical flows are derived from your ui_pages + the registered endpoints, NOT authored by you); 4) `finish()`. NEVER emit one giant inline payload. Your frontend section = ui_pages + ui_components (+ the done_def/feature_inventory scalars). Nothing else