<component_template>
```jsx
// src/pages/TasksPage.jsx
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import { getTasks } from '../services/api';

export default function TasksPage() {
    const [tasks, setTasks] = useState([]);
    const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);
    const [error, setError] = useState(null);

    useEffect(() => {
        getTasks()
            .then(setTasks)
            .catch(err => setError(err.message))
            .finally(() => setLoading(false));
    }, []);

    if (loading) return <div className="p-4">Loading...</div>;
    if (error) return <div className="p-4 text-red-500">{error}</div>;
    if (!tasks.length) return <div className="p-4 text-gray-500">No tasks yet.</div>;

    return (
        <div className="container mx-auto p-4">
            <h1 className="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Tasks</h1>
            <div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
                {tasks.map(task => (
                    <TaskCard key={task.id} task={task} />
                ))}
            </div>
        </div>
    );
}
```
EFFECT-DEPENDENCY RULE (page-hang class): never put a freshly-constructed OBJECT in a
`useEffect` dependency array — `useEffect(..., [startDate])` where the parent derives
`startDate` with `new Date(...)`/`getWeekStart(...)` on every render creates a NEW identity
each render → the effect re-fires → setState → re-render → INFINITE fetch loop → the page
never settles and times out (a real hang the browser gate flags). Depend on stable
PRIMITIVES instead: `[startDate.toISOString()]` / `[weekKey]`, or memoize the object with
`useMemo`. Also import EVERY icon/component you reference in JSX — an unimported
`<Mail/>` builds fine but crashes the page at render (`ReferenceError`).
</component_template>


<map_surface_template>
ONLY when a screen's PRIMARY surface is an interactive geographic map (a Google-Maps-style app: a pan/zoom map with location pins) — build a REAL Leaflet map, never a static image or a CSS box pretending to be a map. Use react-leaflet + OpenStreetMap tiles (both auto-installed once you import them — do NOT edit package.json). The map reads its markers from your places data (GET the places endpoint). Exact pattern:
{% raw %}
```jsx
import { MapContainer, TileLayer, Marker, Popup } from 'react-leaflet';
import 'leaflet/dist/leaflet.css';
import L from 'leaflet';
import markerIcon from 'leaflet/dist/images/marker-icon.png';
import markerIcon2x from 'leaflet/dist/images/marker-icon-2x.png';
import markerShadow from 'leaflet/dist/images/marker-shadow.png';
// REQUIRED default-marker fix — without this every marker is INVISIBLE (bundlers break
// Leaflet's node_modules icon paths). Do it once at module scope.
L.Icon.Default.mergeOptions({ iconUrl: markerIcon, iconRetinaUrl: markerIcon2x, shadowUrl: markerShadow });

export default function MapCanvas({ places = [], center = [37.7749, -122.4194], zoom = 13 }) {
  return (
    // the MapContainer MUST have an explicit height or Leaflet renders 0px tall (blank map)
    <MapContainer center={center} zoom={zoom} style={{ height: '100%', width: '100%' }} scrollWheelZoom>
      <TileLayer
        attribution='&copy; OpenStreetMap contributors'
        url="https://{s}.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png" />
      {places.map(p => (
        <Marker key={p.id} position={[p.lat, p.lng]}>
          <Popup><strong>{p.name}</strong><br/>{p.category} · {p.rating}★</Popup>
        </Marker>
      ))}
    </MapContainer>
  );
}
```
{% endraw %}
RULES: (1) the map's parent element needs a real height (e.g. a flex `<div className="flex-1">` or `h-screen`) or the `height:100%` collapses to 0 and the map is blank. (2) the OSM tile URL `https://{s}.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png` is LEFT VERBATIM — the framework will NOT localize it (it is the live basemap, not a content image). (3) markers come from real data (place lat/lng); a results-list panel and the map share the same places array so a click on a list row can pan/select its marker. (4) do NOT hard-code a Google Maps JavaScript API key or `maps.googleapis.com` — this clone uses free OSM tiles, no key.
</map_surface_template>


<nginx_conf_template>
Ship `nginx.conf.template` (rendered at container start by `start.sh` via `envsubst` of ONLY the named vars — so nginx runtime vars like `$uri`/`$host` survive). The embedded AS lives in the SAME backend, so all of `/api`, `/auth`, `/oauth`, `/.well-known` proxy to `${API_URL}`; they are more specific than the SPA `location /`, so longest-prefix wins regardless of order; do NOT add a `/api/v1` location that rewrites the prefix the backend expects.
```nginx
# nginx.conf.template
server {
    listen ${UI_PORT};
    root /usr/share/nginx/html;
    location /api          { proxy_pass ${API_URL}; proxy_http_version 1.1; proxy_set_header Host $host; }
    location /auth         { proxy_pass ${API_URL}; proxy_http_version 1.1; proxy_set_header Host $host; }
    location /oauth        { proxy_pass ${API_URL}; proxy_http_version 1.1; proxy_set_header Host $host; }
    location /.well-known  { proxy_pass ${API_URL}; proxy_http_version 1.1; proxy_set_header Host $host; }
    location /             { try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html; }    # SPA fallback (least specific)
}
```
```sh
# start.sh
#!/bin/sh
set -e
: "${UI_PORT:=3000}"; : "${API_URL:=http://backend:8080}"
envsubst '${UI_PORT} ${API_URL}' < /etc/nginx/templates/default.conf.template > /etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf
exec nginx -g 'daemon off;'
```
</nginx_conf_template>


